#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/build/index.rst:4
msgid "⏩️ :doc:`Set up email notifications </guides/build/email-notifications>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/build/index.rst:5
msgid ""
"Email notifications can alert you when your builds fail. This is the most"
" simple way to monitor your documentation builds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/build/index.rst:8
msgid "⏩️ :doc:`/guides/build/webhooks`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/build/index.rst:9
msgid ""
"Outgoing webhooks can used to send updates on builds to other services. "
"We show examples using webhooks to connect to popular platforms like "
"Slack and Discord."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/build/index.rst:12
msgid "⏩️ :doc:`Configuring pull request builds </guides/pull-requests>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/build/index.rst:13
msgid ""
"Have your documentation built and access a preview for every :doc:`pull "
"request builds </pull-requests>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/build/index.rst:15
msgid ""
"⏩️ :doc:`Using custom environment variables </guides/environment-"
"variables>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/build/index.rst:16
msgid ""
"Extra environment variables, for instance secrets, may be needed in the "
"build process and can be defined from the project's :term:`dashboard`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/build/index.rst:18
msgid "⏩️ :doc:`Managing versions automatically </guides/automation-rules>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/build/index.rst:19
msgid ""
"Automating your versioning on Read the Docs means you only have to handle"
" your versioning logic in Git. Learn how to define rules to automate "
"creation of new versions on Read the Docs, entirely using your Git "
"repository's version logic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/build/index.rst:23
msgid ""
"⏩️ :doc:`Skip or cancel builds based on conditions </guides/build/skip-"
"or-cancel-builds>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/build/index.rst:24
msgid ""
"Skip builds before they are triggered using automation rules, or cancel a"
" running build from your own commands using the special exit code 183. "
"This helps save resources by avoiding unnecessary documentation builds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/build/index.rst:28
msgid "⏩️ :doc:`Direct upload </guides/build/direct-upload>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/guides/build/index.rst:29
msgid ""
"Build your documentation in GitHub Actions or any other continuous "
"integration service, and upload the result to Read the Docs for hosting."
msgstr ""

